mn limit.\n- `src/sensei_top/api/routes/meta.py`: `decks()` is one query. A `first_played` CTE groups by deck, `LEFT JOIN` attaches it, and `WHERE s.matches_played > 0` drops zero-match decks. The sort order is unchanged. The docstring now explains the exclusion and the grouped pass.\n- `web/src/types/api.ts`: regenerated with `pnpm --dir web gen:types`, not edited by hand.\n- `web/src/lib/deckOverview.ts`: `versionDays` takes `Pick<Deck, 'first_played' | 'first_seen' | 'last_played'>` and starts from `deck.first_played ?? deck.first_seen`. The doc comment explains why.\n\n**Checks**\n- `uv run pytest -q tests/test_api.py`: 183 passed.\n- `uv run ruff check .`: passes after the line wrap.\n- `pnpm --dir web gen:types`: succeeded.\n- `pnpm --dir web test`: 496 passed across 21 files.\n- `pnpm --dir web exec tsc -b`: exit 0.\n- `pnpm --dir web lint`: exit 0.\n\nThe pytest run came before the line wrap in `common.py`. That edit is formatting only and the API tests don't depend on it, but I did not re-run pytest after it. The regenerated `api.ts` came from the pre-wrap model; the schema is identical.\n\nI didn't touch the test files, the MTGO candidates route, the views, or the docs. `SPEC.md` is still untracked in the worktree.", "ttft_ms": 1693, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 60521, "uuid": "5017be07-ffe5-4fc6-9834-c2a18e20dc90", "ttft_stream_ms": 1515, "time_to_request_ms": 506, "first_content_frame_ms": 1515, "queued_turn_count": 0, "result_index": 0}
